{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":22503,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","packSha":"e8a0159364aa6164574069f1ce8c2596a039faf2bb616715cd836c83b990ca1d","packTokens":7639,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":67,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":678,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":907,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":5918,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Replace phone/email-based parts ordering with a self-service ordering portal\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Allow customers to quickly find parts using part numbers, product names, categories, and vehicle information\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Show each customer their applicable pricing and current stock availability\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Reduce manual order-entry work for office staff\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Give customers visibility into order status and invoices\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide staff with operational order queues and delivery information\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide management with basic sales and product reporting\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Maintain an auditable history of orders, invoices, customer accounts, and catalogue changes\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement customer authentication with sign-in, password reset, and account management\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Build product catalogue with search, filtering, categories, and vehicle compatibility\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-11\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement customer-specific pricing and price list management\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-12\",\n  \"text\": \"Manage stock availability with ERP CSV imports\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-13\",\n  \"text\": \"Build basket and checkout workflow with delivery date rules\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-14\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement order management with status tracking and staff editing capabilities\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-15\",\n  \"text\": \"Build customer order history, cancellation, and repeat order functionality\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-16\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement invoice creation, viewing, PDF download, and payment tracking\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-17\",\n  \"text\": \"Build administrative tools for product, user, category, and price list management\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Is the Customer Account Manager role part of the first release?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No: first release has Buyer, Office Staff and Administrator only\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Does a Buyer see every order and invoice of their company, or only the ones they placed? The Buyer section says 'their company's orders', but the Account Manager role adds 'orders placed by other users'.\",\n  \"answer\": \"Buyer sees all orders and invoices of their own company\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Which status changes can staff make after confirmation? Can they skip a status, go back a step, or cancel a Confirmed or Picking order?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Forward only, in order (Confirmed → Picking → Out for delivery → Delivered); staff may cancel any order not yet Delivered\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Under 'where permitted', when may staff change the delivery date or address before confirmation?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Always before confirmation, limited to the customer's addresses and dates valid under the cutoff rule\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"What happens to a customer company's users and open orders when the company is set inactive?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Its users cannot sign in or order; existing orders and invoices stay visible to staff\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Buyers see all of their company's orders (answer Q-2). Can a Buyer also cancel or repeat a Received order that a colleague placed, or that staff created for the company?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Any Buyer of the company may cancel or repeat any company order that is eligible\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"With no Customer Account Manager in the first release (answer Q-1), can Buyers add or edit their company's delivery addresses, or do only staff/admins manage them?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only staff/admins manage addresses; Buyers choose from existing ones\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"For an inactive customer company (answer Q-5), can staff still move its open orders forward, create new orders for it, and have invoices created when its orders are delivered?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Open orders continue as normal and invoices are still created; staff cannot create new orders for the company\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must allow users to sign in with email and password, starting an authenticated session and returning the user's role when credentials match an active account.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must reject sign-in attempts with unknown emails or wrong passwords using one identical invalid-credentials error message, returning no session token.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must lock an account for 15 minutes after 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts, rejecting all sign-ins during the lock with a temporary-lock error.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must reject sign-in and all requests, including order submission, from users who are deactivated or belong to an inactive customer company, even if they hold valid existing sessions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must invalidate a user's session token when the user signs out.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must reject with status 401, without returning any record data, any request to endpoints other than sign-in, password reset and invitation acceptance that lacks a valid session token.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must reject with status 403 any request to an endpoint outside a user's role capabilities, with Administrator including all Office Staff capabilities.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must restrict a signed-in Buyer to orders, invoices, prices, delivery addresses and account data belonging to their own customer company, returning 404 for other companies' records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must respond identically to password reset requests whether or not the email exists, sending a single-use reset email valid for a configurable period (default 1 hour) only when the account is active (including temporarily locked) and its company, if any, is active.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must allow a user to set a new password via an unexpired, unused reset link, replacing the password, invalidating the link and clearing any sign-in lock.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must reject password changes via reset links that are expired, already used, or belong to pending, deactivated, or inactive-company users, keeping the password and any lock unchanged.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must allow administrators to invite Buyers (linked to a company) or Office Staff, creating a pending account and sending an invitation email valid for a configurable period (default 7 days).\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must allow administrators to invite users with the Administrator role, creating a pending account and sending an invitation email.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must activate an invited user's account when they set a password through an unexpired invitation link.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must allow administrators to resend invitations for pending accounts, invalidating all previous invitation links and sending a new invitation email.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators list users with role, company and status, assign Buyers to companies, and deactivate/reactivate users without deleting their orders or invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators change a user's role between Buyer and Office Staff.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators change a user's role to Administrator.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must reject reactivation of a deactivated user whose customer company is inactive.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Buyers search the catalogue by text term across product name, code, part number and brand, case-insensitively, returning only active products.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Buyers filter the catalogue by category, combined with search terms, returning only active matching products, and show all active products again once the filter is cleared.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Buyers search by vehicle attributes (make, model, year, engine, fuel type, variant) in any combination, returning only active products whose compatibility entries match all supplied values.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must return, for catalogue listing, only active products with image, name, code, manufacturer, unit of sale, pack size, Buyer's price and stock status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must return, for a single opened active product, its image, name, code, manufacturer, description, unit, pack size, Buyer's price, stock status and compatible vehicles.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must price products and order/basket lines from the price list currently assigned to the Buyer's company at request time, applying changed assignments going forward.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Office Staff view the unit price a given customer company pays for a product, from that company's assigned price list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 27,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must show a product with no price on a company's assigned price list as 'Price on request' and reject adding it to a basket or order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 28,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators create, rename and deactivate price lists; set, edit and remove at most one price per product per list; and assign an active price list to a customer company.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 29,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must leave unit prices on existing orders and invoices unchanged when a price list price or company assignment changes later.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 30,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must derive stock status as Out of stock at or below zero or never imported, Low stock up to the configured threshold, and In stock above it.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 31,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must, on a scheduled ERP stock import of a valid CSV, update quantities and stock status for known products and record a successful import log with row counts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 32,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must skip unknown product identifiers in an otherwise valid import, applying other rows and listing skipped identifiers in the log.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 33,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must keep stock quantities unchanged and log a failed import with a reason when the CSV is missing, unreadable, empty, lacks a required column, or has invalid quantities.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 34,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let staff and administrators list stock imports with time, status, rows-applied count, skipped identifiers and failure reason.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 35,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must never send create, update or delete requests to the ERP system.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 36,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must show staff, on a product, its imported stock quantity, stock status, last successful import time and price per price list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 37,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must reject basket, order creation or amendment quantities exceeding available stock, or additions of out-of-stock products, with an error stating available quantity.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 38,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must maintain a per-session Buyer basket allowing adding, quantity changes (minimum 1), and removal of lines, returning line prices, totals and subtotal.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 39,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must calculate the earliest delivery date as the next working day before a configurable cutoff (default 14:00) or the working day after that otherwise, skipping non-working dates, in the configured timezone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 40,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must accept only a working day within the earliest-to-maximum delivery window as a valid delivery date, checked at submission, offering exactly those dates and rejecting others with an error naming the delivery date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 41,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must reject a delivery address not belonging to the order's company, with an error naming the delivery address field.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 42,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must re-check availability, stock limits and current pricing for every basket line at order submission, rejecting the submission and listing affected lines if any fail.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 43,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must show Buyers a final checkout review page with lines, prices, totals, subtotal, address, date and note before submission.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 44,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must, on valid order submission, create an order with a sequential prefixed number, order-time prices, copied address, delivery date, optional note, Received status, and a first timeline entry, then clear the basket.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 45,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must reject order submissions by inactive-company users, deactivated users, or for inactive companies by staff, creating no order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 46,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must append a timeline entry with status, timestamp and actor (user or System) on every order status change.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 47,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must send order emails to the placing Buyer if still active and linked to the company, and otherwise to the company's contact email, including for staff-created orders.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 48,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Buyers list all orders of their company, including colleagues' and staff-created orders, with key fields, filterable by status and date range.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 49,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let a Buyer of the order's company or staff open an order to view its number, dates, address, status, timeline, lines, totals, note and amendments.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 50,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let a Buyer cancel their company's Received-status order, setting it Cancelled with a timeline entry.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 51,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must reject Buyer cancellation of non-Received orders, with an error directing them to contact the distributor office.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 52,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let a Buyer repeat a past order, adding still-orderable lines to the basket at current price and original quantity (capped at stock, flagged if reduced), flagging unavailable lines, without creating an order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 53,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let staff list all customers' orders with key fields, filterable by customer, date range and status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 54,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let staff search customers by partial name or account number, and open a customer to view its details, addresses, price list, users, status, orders and invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 55,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let staff edit a Received order only, limited to quantities, line removal, note, address (same company) and delivery date (valid at edit time).\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 56,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must record staff quantity changes or line removals as amendments with old/new values, staff and time, and email the order recipient listing the changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 57,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let staff confirm a Received order with valid lines and address, setting it Confirmed with a timeline entry, or reject listing failing lines otherwise.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 58,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must send a confirmation email on order confirmation containing order number, lines, total, address, date and any pre-confirmation quantity changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 59,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let staff advance order status only through the sequence Confirmed, Picking, Out for delivery, Delivered (or cancellation), recording a timeline entry, rejecting other transitions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 60,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must email the order recipient when status changes to Out for delivery, naming the order and stating it is out for delivery.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 61,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must require a reason when staff cancel or reject a non-Delivered, non-Cancelled order, recording the reason, staff and time, and emailing the recipient with the reason.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 62,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let staff submit orders on behalf of active companies under the same price, stock, address and date rules as Buyer orders, marked as staff-created.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 63,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must keep an inactive company's existing orders and invoices visible and let staff progress, cancel and invoice its open orders.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 64,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let staff export a CSV delivery list for a given date (default today) with one row per non-Cancelled order due that date, including specified fields.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 65,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must show staff a dashboard with counts of orders by Received, Picking, Out for delivery status, orders due today, and Unpaid/Overdue invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 66,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must show staff a dashboard count of Confirmed-status orders.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 67,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must show staff a dashboard count of failed stock imports since the last success.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 68,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must show staff the latest stock import result, including failure time and reason, when it failed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 69,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must create one invoice when an order becomes Delivered, with a sequential prefixed number, customer and billing details, order reference, order-time lines, net/tax/gross totals and Unpaid status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 70,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must report invoice payment status as Unpaid, then Overdue after a configurable number of days, and Paid once payment is recorded.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 71,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let users list invoices with key fields, restricted to their own company for Buyers and all companies for staff.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 72,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Office Staff list and view all invoices, filterable by customer and payment status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 73,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let a Buyer of the invoice's company or staff download an invoice PDF containing invoice and order details, totals, payment status and distributor branding.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 74,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let staff mark an Unpaid or Overdue invoice as paid with a payment date no later than today, recording the date and staff, storing no card data and never contacting payment providers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 75,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators add, edit and retire products with specified fields, keeping retired products out of the catalogue but on existing orders/invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 76,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators create, rename and retire single-level categories and assign products to them, hiding retired categories from Buyers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 77,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators upload a product image, replacing any previous image, only accepting JPEG, PNG or WebP files up to 10 MB.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 78,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators add and remove vehicle compatibility entries on a product, with any number of entries allowed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 79,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators create and edit customer companies with specified fields including price list assignment and active status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 80,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must restrict adding, editing and removing a company's delivery addresses to staff/administrators, while letting Buyers view their own company's addresses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 81,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators view and change system settings including cutoff time, timezone, non-working dates, maximum delivery days, low-stock threshold, overdue days, tax rate, number prefixes, link validity periods, and invoice branding.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 82,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must store creator and last-changer identities and timestamps on orders, invoices, companies, users, products, categories and price lists, returning them to administrators.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 83,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Office Staff and Administrators request a sales report for a date range, optionally filtered by customer, showing order counts, net totals and product sales, both on-screen and as CSV.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 84,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must reject an administrator's attempt to deactivate their own account or change their own role, leaving the account unchanged.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}